| Request ID | Target identified by host/page | `reason` | `error` summary |
|---:|---|---|---|
| 1 | kva.se, 2015 Chemistry news page | `redirect_loop` | Error repeats the requested URL. |
| 13 | enseignementsup-recherche.gouv.fr, Sauvage 2016 page | `http_status` | HTTP 403 for requested URL. |
| 22 | axios.com, 2018 Chemistry announcement | `http_status` | HTTP 403 for requested URL. |
| 21 | kva.se, 2017 Chemistry news page | `redirect_loop` | Error repeats the requested URL. |
| 30 | princeton.edu, “princetons-david-macmillan-receives…” | `http_status` | HTTP 403 for requested URL. |
| 29 | prizeatlas.org, Charpentier page | `download_error` | SSL certificate verification failed: hostname mismatch for `www.prizeatlas.org`; `_ssl.c:1010`. |
| 42 | investing.com, 2024 Chemistry announcement | `http_status` | HTTP 403 for requested URL. |
| 45 | mdpi.com, announcement 9565 | `http_status` | HTTP 403 for requested URL. |
| 20 | washingtonpost.com, 2017 Chemistry announcement | `download_error` | `[Errno 32] Broken pipe`. |
| 53 | tap.info.tn, president-saied page | `download_error` | SSL certificate verification failed: unable to get local issuer certificate; `_ssl.c:1010`. |
| 58 | geniuses.club, Bawendi page | `http_status` | HTTP 403 for requested URL. |
| 59 | vietnamtimes.thoidai.com.vn, Ekimov article with encoded suffix | `http_status` | HTTP 404 reported for the site root, differing from the requested article URL. |
| 56 | jeantet.ch, Henderson page | `redirect_loop` | Error repeats the requested URL. |

The failure breakdown is **7 HTTP-status failures**—six 403s and one 404—**3 redirect loops**, and **3 download errors**—two certificate failures and one broken pipe. These are the same 13 failures represented in `fetches`, not 13 additional failures.

Every fetch record includes:

- `id` and `url`: attempt identifier and requested resource.
- `focus`: intended extraction scope.
- `source`: always `backend`.
- `status`: `succeeded` or `failed`.
- `fetch_path`: always `direct-readable-v1`.
- `text_policy`: always `unicode-layout-controls-v1`.
- `receipt_id`: an opaque receipt identifier, present on every attempt, including failures.
- `reason` and `error`: supplied on failed attempts.

The focus distribution is:

| Fetch IDs | Focus |
|---|---|
| 1–10 | Laureates, citizenship/nationality, award-time affiliation, exact motivation |
| 11 | Empty string |
| 12–45 | Explicit nationality/citizenship of Chemistry laureates |
| 46–49 | Explicit nationality/citizenship |
| 50–55 | Explicit citizenship/nationality, including multiple citizenships |
| 56–60 | Explicit citizenship/nationality and award-time affiliation |

Fetch success is **47/60, or 78.3%**. A receipt or successful status establishes recorded retrieval behavior, not that the retrieved material answered the requested focus.

For citations, `path` identifies the cited output location, `url` identifies its source, and `fetched` and `verbatim` record the checker’s two citation outcomes. Each of the 28 rows has exactly 11 citation records:

- Five cell paths: `laureate`, `year`, `nationality`, `affiliation_at_award`, and `prize_motivation`.
- One `question` path.
- Five `columns/0` through `columns/4` paths.

That yields **140 cell citations plus 168 constraint-location citations = 308**. All 308 pass both recorded flags; none has a false or missing flag.

The complete citation-source mapping can be summarized using fetch IDs. For each row, the default source covers every citation except the two nationality locations where an override appears:

| Rows | Default source fetch ID | Nationality override fetch ID |
|---|---:|---|
| 0–2 | 11 | None |
| 3–5 | 2 | Row 3: 12; row 4: 50; row 5: 14 |
| 6–8 | 4 | Row 6: 18; row 7: 19; row 8: 46 |
| 9–11 | 3 | Row 9: 51; row 10: 47; row 11: 23 |
| 12–14 | 5 | Row 12: 24; row 13: 26; row 14: 25 |
| 15–16 | 6 | Row 15: 27; row 16: 49 |
| 17–18 | 7 | Row 17: 33; row 18: 31 |
| 19–21 | 8 | Row 19: 35; rows 20–21: 34 |
| 22–24 | 9 | Row 22: 57; row 23: 41; row 24: 38 |
| 25–27 | 10 | All three rows: 43 |

There are **32 distinct cited URLs**: ten Nobel-site sources and 22 other sources. Nobel-site sources account for 258 citation records; external nationality sources account for 50. All cited URLs correspond to successful fetches; none corresponds to a failed attempt. Fifteen successfully fetched URLs are not cited. Repeated citations across cell and constraint paths do not constitute independent corroboration.

For constraint coverage, `row` identifies rows 0–27; `constraint` is `question` or one of `columns/0`–`columns/4`; `checked` records that a check occurred; and `agent_verdict` records the agent’s judgment. All **28 × 6 = 168** combinations are present and true, with no coverage gaps in that represented grid. These are positive agent verdicts, not independent validation of the original requirements.

The evidence therefore supports complete recorded citation and constraint coverage despite retrieval problems. It does **not** prove factual accuracy, source entailment, correct interpretation of nationality versus citizenship, award-time accuracy, or completeness against the original task: the answer values, supporting passages, original constraints, and checker implementation are absent.

Finally, `source: backend` locates the reported fetch failures in the retrieval layer; it does not prove the backend itself caused every failure. Remote access restrictions, certificates, redirects, transport faults, or URL handling may be involved. Request 59’s encoded suffix and differing error URL warrant inspection, but do not establish agent error. Likewise, stalled discovery signals alone do not establish poor search judgment. No specific agent error is demonstrated by this audit.

